From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: Tim May's Social Darwinism

Ray Cromwell writes:

>   I agree of course, but I think the problem is that long tirades on
> traditional liberal heros will eventually provoke a flame war.

My "long tirade" was in response to a question---some would call it a
"whine," though I mean no aspersions against Betsy--of the sort: "But
what about the poor?" My answer, which I don't think is a flame, is
basically this: "Tell the poor that no one owes them a living. Tell
the poor that they'd better find a job or a trade or something that
other people want to pay them to do. Otherwise, too bad. No work, no eat."

> I could certainly start a flame war by saying "anyone who belives in
> the supernatural is an irrational fruitcake who deserves biological
> extinction when it comes" and if I did so, the coming flames in my email
> box would be rightly deserved because I know how people will respond.
> There are certain subjects which are instant hot buttons for some people,
> like criticizing racial minorities, or as you found out, making statements
> about other sexualities. 

Sorr, Ray, this is nonsense. Extropians are free to point out the
absurdity of welfare systems, religious systems, supernatural beliefs,
astrology, whatever. Even to discuss the evidence about racial
differences in intelligence. And especially to discuss theories about
why women appear to be less technically-oriented than men are and why
men are less communication- and feeling-oriented than women are.

If not on this List, where? 

(And don't forget that Amara _called_ for this discusson of gender
roles, differences, "women's issues," etc.  She even claimed to have
learned some "facts" about how men, especially technical men, use
debate, argument, and creative extrapolation (bullshitting, which
really isn't, as I argued) to succeed in many industries. She and the
other women may feel my remarks are politically incorrect and
misogynistic, but I view them as a truth that needs to be
discussed....vivre la difference.)

>   Tim, you're a little older so your perspective is different. I grew up
> in a culture, in a public school, which repeated like mantra: never
> blame the victim, it's society's fault, bums are people too, etc.
> And I suspect many other people have absorbed these values. So while
> it may be right to condemn theives, bums, welfare moms, etc, it's still
> going fire people up.  

Political correctness, which Ray if referring to here, should be the
_last_ thing we practice here. Yes, we have "our own" ideas of what is
politically correct....all cultures do. We, for example, tend to
axiomatically reject arguments that the individual lives only for the
good of the Society. So be it. But adopting the mainstream notions of
political correctness seems too bizarrre to even contemplate.

I intend to continue speaking my mind. I really don't care what sacred
cows I offend. (And I think the Extropians are "tolerant" of many
differences in opinion. I, for example, am not signed up for any form
of cryonic suspension, and yet I am not insulted or chastised for
these "Extropianly Incorrect" views, nor do I chastise others for
their faith in Alcor and the like.)

Arguments should be made for positions, and refutations.

The claims in recent days by Price, Starr, and others, that my views
are tantamount to calling for the extermination of the poor and
non-white races is _classic_ argumentum ad hominem.

And the claim that discussing gender and racial differences, which
surely exist to some degree or another, will somehow offend and
possibly drive away people is ludicrous. Should we _only_ discuss such
empty issues as the arrival date of the Singularity?

I'm really beginning to see how deeply the younger folks on the List
have been affected by the last couple of decades of "never hurt
anyone's feelings" ideology. Instead of calling a spade a spade
(whoops, can't use that expression anymore, can I?, people step
gingerly around the real issues. Things get worse because nobody will
say the Emperor is naked....even here on this List, of all places, we
see this pussyfooting around.

Folks, recognize that we are an elite. Ubermenschen (assuming the use
of a fine German word is not verboten by an ersatz Zeitgeist).
Superior ideas.

Yes, some ideas and some values are "better" than others. I don't
claim a supernatural or "logical" (a la Rand) origin for this
statement, but it's something we know. Or at least I hope most of us
know.

It's what the "Extropian Principles" are all about. If you don't
believe some values are indeed superior to others, I suspect you don't
belong on this List.

And if you do believe in the strength of certain values, then you
should certainly be willing to forthrightly argue for them and not
cower because the views might "offend" someone (whose values are
likely anyway to stick a gun in your face and say "give me your
money"). 

For those who genuinely disagree, or have some questions, engage them
in discussion. For those who dismiss you as a Nazi, who claim you are
calling for concentration camps and gas chambers, tell them to go to
hell and put them in your ::exclude file. It is working for me, as a
growing number of List simps and wimps have entered my ::exclude file.


--Tim May, who has been politically incorrect since at least 1964.


