necessarily very subtle -- the hand is *invisible*, after all.  Human 
behavior is complex, which is why attempts to analyze and control it in 
a simplistic manner (like the centralized planning of socialism) have 
never succeeded for any length of time.  So I believe that we  
libertarians must master the art of subtle argument if we hope to 
persuade anybody but ourselves.

