For me, the main point of this list is to discuss ways to improve our 
chances of living as long as we want, in the kind of culture that suits us.
Although few of us have warm feelings for the welfare state, I hate to see
name-calling attacks on welfare recipients, retarded people, and the mentally
ill on the List, and I am especially concerned that anyone would believe that
hatred of such groups is anything like an axiomatic, core belief of 
Extropianism.

And let's not confuse dismantling the welfare state with cold-heartedness
toward the unfortunate.  I will always be willing to donate some of my time 
and/or money to those who had the misfortune to be born retarded or mentally
ill.  I do not ask Tim, or anyone else, to do the same.  But please don't
advertise personal feelings about the poor, retarded, clinically depressed, 
et al., as part of the Extropian philosophy.

-- Simon!

